{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 12, "high": 22, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 60,
      "why": "Only a fully pipelined (1 result/cycle) datapath can plausibly reach 400 MSPS single-lane; m=1 gives the shortest per-stage logic and thus the highest Fmax. Ranges bracket the accuracy boundary (W>=14, N>=14 for 2^-12) so the search can find the minimum-LUT feasible point."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 12, "high": 22, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "m", "low": 2, "high": 4, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 40,
      "why": "Still 1 result/cycle, but registering every m stages trades Fmax for fewer FFs; m=2..4 keeps the combinational path short enough that 400 MSPS may remain reachable while potentially reducing area. Included to cover the area/throughput trade-off on the front."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The 400 MSPS single-lane constraint rules out iterative and unrolled_k (their multi-cycle-per-result schedules would need Fmax far above what Artix-7 can deliver). Only pipelined and pipelined_m produce one result per cycle, so throughput equals Fmax and the search must focus there. Accuracy (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) requires roughly W>=14 and N>=14, so the ranges are centred on that boundary (W 12..20, N 12..22) with small guard-bit ranges, letting the optimiser find the minimum-LUT design that still meets both constraints. Round 1 spends most budget on the m=1 pipelined family (best Fmax) and the rest on pipelined_m with small m to map the area/throughput trade-off."
}
